{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs5UfdUq4oXYGG1wyHQz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dependency chain now shows up in resolution errors for indirect requirements, and the new tests pass. Running `tests/test_bootstrapper_iterative.py` gives 116 passed and 1 failed. The failure is `TestPhasePrepareSource::test_constraint_logged_when_present`, an empty-`caplog` assertion in code I didn't touch. It also fails with my changes stashed, so it was already broken.\n\nI couldn't run ruff or mypy: `.venv/bin/ruff` doesn't exist. The new parametrized test has a few lines over the formatter's length limit, so `hatch run lint:fix` is worth running before you commit.\n\n**What changed in `_bootstrapper.py`:**\n- **`_dependency_chain_suffix`:** builds `\" (dependency chain: a==1 -> b==2 -> <wi.req>)\"` from `wi.why_snapshot`.\n- **`_enrich_resolution_error`:** appends the suffix for `Resolve` items with a non-empty `why_snapshot`. `ResolverException` and `RuntimeError` keep their type, and anything else becomes `RuntimeError(\"<TypeName>: <msg><suffix>\")`. Other phases and top-level requirements get back the same exception object.\n- **`_handle_phase_error`:** enriches the error first, so test mode and multiple-versions mode record the enriched version. In normal mode it raises the enriched exception without `from`, inside the original handler, so `__context__` is the original and `__cause__` stays unset. When nothing was enriched it still does a bare `raise`.\n- **Subclasses:** a `ResolverException` subclass such as `ResolutionImpossible` comes back as a plain `ResolverException`, so its causes data is lost.\n- **Import:** I added a module-level `import resolvelib.resolvers`.\n\n**New tests:**\n- The chain suffix text.\n- The three exception-type mappings.\n- Unchanged return for top-level requirements and for non-`Resolve` phases.\n- Normal-mode raise: `__cause__` is `None` and `__context__` is the original.\n- Enriched message recorded in test mode and in multiple-versions mode.\n\nI haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6312,"cache_read_input_tokens":60415,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6312},"output_tokens":734,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"83b43240-bc5a-4cf5-8310-d7ef3096da1e","uuid":"facfabe2-1be9-4ca6-967e-cbfbedda2843","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:43:56.074Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs5UfLNHxmxwvqGjq87B"}
